> >     rightfall = (uright && !uright->cursed && (!welded(uwep)));
> 
> Could it be a bug that rightfall doesn't check the non-nullness of
> uwep, as leftfall does, like:
> 
>  rightfall = (uright && !uright->cursed && (!uwep || !welded(uwep)));
> 
> That could lead to some unexpected results in the code below what
> you show, where the right ring is dropped, if I read that code
> correctly.

rightfall doesn't check itself, but welded() will do it for it:

welded(obj)
register struct obj *obj;
{
        if (obj && obj == uwep && will_weld(obj)) {
                obj->bknown = TRUE;
                return 1;
        }
        return 0;
}

leftfall's check is guarding bimanual() (which doesn't), not welded().

